$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Solution of 10a (300 mg, 0.54 mmol) and NCS (44 mg, 0.11 mmol) in
pyridine (20 mL) was stirred for 2 hours at 70°C and then was evaporated.
The residue was redissolved in DCM (50 mL) and washed with water (2 × 20
mL). The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated. The crude
product was purified by column chromatography (40 g of silica gel,
hexanes →hexanes-EtOAc, 1:1). 11 (300 mg) as a white powder. Yield 94%.
m.p. 161-164°C; R f (A) 0.92; MS (ESI) m/z [M+H]+ calcd 590.1; found
590.2.
