$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6-Chlorobenzoxazolone (XVa) Benzoxazolone (1.4 g, 0.01 mol) and NCS (1.4
g, 0.01 mol) were added to 15 ml of acetic acid and stirred for 7 days at
ambient temperatures. The reaction course was monitored by gas
chromatography. Upon completion of the reaction, the mixture was poured
into 500 ml of water, stirred 15 min, and the product recovered by
filtration. After washing with water and drying at 90 °C overnight, XVa
was obtained. Crystallization from aqueous ethanol did not alter the
melting point. Yield 1.6 g (94%). M.p. 194-195 °C.(Ref. [28] m.p. 194-195
°C, yield 81%). 1H-NMR: δ = 11.70 (s, H-NH), 7.45 (d, 7-H), 7.21 (dd,
5-H), 7.07 (d, 4-H), J4,5 =7.87 Hz, J5,7 = 1.65 Hz.
