$DATUM Ethyl
5-Chloro-3-(1,3-dioxoisoindolin-2-yl)-6-methoxy-4-methylthieno[2,3-b]pyridine-2-carboxylate
(30). Compound 29 (500 mg, 1.26 mmol), N-chlorosuccinimide (337 mg, 2.52
mmol), and 3 drops of concentrated HCl were refluxed in acetonitrile (10
mL) for 1.5 h. The solvent was then removed in vacuo and the resulting
residue redissolved in chloroform (50 mL) and washed with water (3 × 20
mL) and brine (50 mL). The organic layer was then dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate, filtered, and evaporated to dryness to give the compound.
Yield: (506 mg, 93%), white solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 1.12 (t, J 7.1 Hz,
3H), 2.49 (s, 3H), 4.13 (s, 3H), 4.21 (q, J 7.1 Hz, 2H), 7.85 (m, 2H),
8.01 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 13.9 (CH3), 14.7 (CH3), 55.4 (CH3), 61.9
(CH2), 118.8 (C), 124.3 (CH), 125.1 (C), 127.0 (C), 127.4 (C), 132.4 (C),
134.9 (CH), 143.0 (C), 155.9 (C), 159.5 (C), 160.9 (C), 167.6 (C).
