$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 6a (500 mg, 0.78 mmol) in DCM (50 mL) bromine (48 μl,
0.94 mmol) in CCl4 (10 mL) was added dropwise at 0°C over 10 minutes.
After 15 minutes of stirring, the reaction mixture was washed with satd.
NaHCO3 solution (2 × 30 mL), dried, and evaporated. Purification of the
crude product by column chromatography (50 g of silica gel, hexanes→
hexanes-EtOAc, 1:1). 8a (520 mg) as a white powder. Yield 92%. m.p.
91-93°C; R f (F) 0.62; MS (ESI) m/z [M+H]+ calcd 719.0, 717.0; found
719.4, 717.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, dropwise addition of bromine/carbon tetrachloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and cytotoxic activity of novel
5-substituted-1-(β-L-arabinofuranosyl) pyrimidine nucleosides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sendula, Robert; Orban, Erika; Hudecz, Ferenc; Sagi, Gyula; Jablonkai,
Istvan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Nucleosides, Nucleotides & Nucleic Acids (2012), 31(6), 482-500

