$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 14a (350 mg, 0.55 mmol) in CHCl3 (20 mL) was added the
solution of Br2 (60 μl, 1.10 mmol) in CCl4 (10 mL) dropwise over 10
minutes at ice-bath temperature. After 15 minutes stirring, the solution
was washed with water (2 × 30 mL). The organic layer dried over Na2SO4
was filtered and evaporated. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (50 g of silica gel, hexanes→hexanes-EtOAc, 1:1). 16a (360
mg) as a yellow powder. Yield 91%. m.p. 120-122°C; R f (A) 0.46; MS (ESI)
m/z [M+Na]+ calcd 740.1, 738.1, 7; found 740.3, 738.3.
