$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a stirring solution of crude
arylthiazol-2-yl-amine (0.42 mmol) in acetic acid was added bromine in
acetic acid (0.42 mmol). The reaction was further stirred for 1 h at room
temperature after which the solvent was removed in vacuum. The resulting
residue was purified by HPLC (C18 column, eluted with CH3CN/H2O with
0.035% TFA) to give (5-bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-aryl-amine as a solid. Yields
varied from 20% to 90%. (5-Bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-(4-iodo-phenyl)-amine (9),
yield 90% 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 7.32 (s, 1H), 7.41 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.61
(d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 10.44 (s, 1H); m/z [M++1] 380.8.
