acetic acid (0.42 mmol). The reaction was further stirred for 1 h at room
temperature after which the solvent was removed in vacuum. The resulting
residue was purified by HPLC (C18 column, eluted with CH3CN/H2O with
0.035% TFA) to give (5-bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-aryl-amine as a solid. Yields
varied from 20% to 90%. (4-Bromo-phenyl)-(5-bromo-thiazol-2-yl)-amine
(8), yield 90% 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 7.31 (s, 1H), 7.46 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz),
7.56 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 10.54 (s, 1H); m/z [M++1] 334.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Selective Aminothiazole Aurora Kinase Inhibitors
