$DATUM 10-Chlorobenzo[h]quinoline (2a). N-Chlorosuccinimide (101 mg, 0.758 mmol,
1.20 equiv) was added to a solution of benzo[h]quinoline (10) (113 mg,
0.632 mmol, 1.00 equiv) and Pd(OAc)2(7.1 mg, 0.032 mmol, 0.050 equiv) in
CH3CN (5.0 mL). The reaction mixture was heated at 100 °C for 50 hours.
The reaction mixture was cooled and solvent was removed in vacuo. The
residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel eluting with hexanes
/ benzene (1:1) to afford 121 mg of the title compound (90% yield). Rf =
0.32 (hexanes/Et2O 9:1 (v/v)). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 9.12
(dd, J = 4.4 Hz, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.19 (dd, J = 8.3 Hz, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.84
(td, J = 7.3 Hz, J = 1.0 Hz, 2H), 7.80 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.72 (d, J =
8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.59-7.55 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ):
147.63, 146.49, 136.32, 135.65, 132.34, 131.53, 128.14, 127.67, 127.60,
127.55, 127.54, 126.62, 121.71. Mass Spectrometry: HRMS-FIA (m/z): calcd
for [C13H8NCl+H], 214.0418. Found, 214.0418.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, literature prepn.
